  "description": "\"Yuji\" is a series of fonts digitizing handwriting by the calligrapher Yuji Kataoka. Akebono is a \"Hentaigana\" font which contains stylistic alternate versions of the standard Hiragana set that were abandoned in 1900 during a script reform. As there are no Hentaigana for Katakana, no Katakana are included. Latin is all-caps / small caps. Fonts in the Yuji Family: Yuji Hentaigana Akari Yuji Boku Yuji Mai Yuji Syuku To contribute to the project, visit github.com/Kinutafontfactory/Yuji",
